# Field table: IEX (Investors Exchange) DEEP+ over IEX-TP, and DEEP+ SNAP.
#
# Documents (public, https://www.iex.io/resources/trading/market-data):
#   TP    IEX Transport Specification, Version 1.25, May 12, 2017
#   DPLS  IEX DEEP+ Specification, Version 1.06, October 8, 2026
#   SNAP  IEX DEEP+ SNAP Specification, Version 1.07, October 8, 2026
#
# Every integer is little-endian (TP p.5, Data Types; DPLS p.5; SNAP p.4).
# Strings are ASCII, left justified, space filled on the right (DPLS p.5).
# Price is a signed 8-byte fixed-point number with 4 implied decimals (DPLS p.5).
# Timestamp is signed 8-byte nanoseconds since the POSIX epoch, UTC (DPLS p.5).
#
# Framing (TP p.5-7): a UDP payload is one IEX-TP segment: a 40-byte header,
# then MessageCount message blocks, each a 2-byte length that excludes itself
# followed by that many bytes of message data. The DEEP+ section below takes
# that 2-byte length as its @length_prefix; DEEP+ offsets are 0-based from the
# Message Type byte, as the DEEP+ tables give them.
#
# SNAP (TCP) tables put Message Length at offset 0 and Message Type at offset 2.
# Here the length is the @length_prefix, so every SNAP offset below is the
# spec's offset minus 2; each description gives the spec's offset.
@venue iex
@endian little
@pad space
@type Byte uint
@type Short uint
@type Integer uint
@type Long int
@type Price int
@type Timestamp int
@type String char
# SNAP Authentication Token: typed Byte in the spec, described as a left
# justified string space padded on the right (SNAP p.7).
@type Token char
@type Bytes bytes

### tp::from_iex

MessageType - 0 0 # SegmentHeader: IEX-TP header at the start of every outbound segment (UDP payload), multicast or gap-fill response (TP v1.25, p.5, IEX-TP Header)
@size 40
Version Byte 0 1 # 1, version of the transport specification
Reserved Byte 1 1 # (Reserved)
MessageProtocolID Short 2 2 # Higher-layer protocol; DEEP+ is 0x8005 (DPLS p.4), DEEP is 0x8004
ChannelID Integer 4 4 # Stream of sequenced messages; same Channel ID from several sources means duplicates by sequence number (p.6)
SessionID Integer 8 4 # Session; a message is identified by Session ID and sequence number (p.6)
PayloadLength Short 12 2 # Bytes of payload after this header; excludes the header (p.6)
MessageCount Short 14 2 # Message blocks in the payload; 0 for a heartbeat or gap-fill test response (p.6, p.7)
StreamOffset Long 16 8 # Byte offset of the payload in the session's data stream (p.6)
FirstMessageSequenceNumber Long 24 8 # Sequence number of the first message; later ones are numbered implicitly; in a heartbeat, the next sequence number (p.6, p.7)
SendTime Timestamp 32 8 # Send time of the segment, ns since epoch UTC

### tp::to_iex

MessageType - 0 0 # GapFillRequestHeader: retransmission request, UDP or TCP unicast to a gap fill server; followed by RequestRangeCount range blocks (TP v1.25, p.8, Gap Fill Request Header)
@size 16
Version Byte 0 1 # 1
RequestType Byte 1 1 # 1 sequenced messages, 2 bytestream; DEEP+ supports 1 only (DPLS p.7, p.10)
MessageProtocolID Short 2 2 # 0x8005 for DEEP+
ChannelID Integer 4 4 # Channel the request is for
SessionID Integer 8 4 # Current session, taken from a multicast segment header (p.8)
RequestRangeCount Integer 12 4 # Range blocks that follow; 0 for a UDP gap fill test request (p.8)

MessageType - 0 0 # RequestRangeSequenced: one requested range when RequestType is 1; ranges must not overlap and must increase (TP v1.25, p.9, Request Range Block (Sequenced Messages))
@size 16
FirstMessageSequenceNumber Long 0 8 # First sequence number requested, inclusive
LastMessageSequenceNumber Long 8 8 # Last sequence number requested, inclusive

MessageType - 0 0 # RequestRangeBytestream: one requested range when RequestType is 2; not supported by DEEP+ (TP v1.25, p.9, Request Range Block (Bytestream))
@size 16
StartingStreamOffset Long 0 8 # First byte requested, inclusive
EndingStreamOffset Long 8 8 # Last byte requested, inclusive

### deepplus::from_iex
@length_prefix 2 exclusive

MessageType S 0 1 # SystemEvent: market or feed event, one per type per channel per session (DPLS v1.06, p.13, System Event Message)
@size 10
SystemEvent Byte 1 1 # O start of messages, S start of system hours, R start of regular market hours, M end of regular market hours, E end of system hours, C end of messages
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the system event

MessageType D 0 1 # SecurityDirectory: pre-market spin of all IEX-listed securities, then changes (DPLS v1.06, p.14, Security Directory Message)
@size 31
Flags Byte 1 1 # 0x80 test security, 0x40 when issued, 0x20 ETP (Appendix A, p.28)
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the security information
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
RoundLotSize Integer 18 4 # Shares in a round lot
AdjustedPOCPrice Price 22 8 # Corporate-action adjusted previous official closing price
LULDTier Byte 30 1 # 0 not applicable, 1 Tier 1 NMS stock, 2 Tier 2 NMS stock

MessageType H 0 1 # TradingStatus: pre-market spin for all securities, then changes; absent from the spin means operationally halted (DPLS v1.06, p.15-16, Trading Status Message)
@size 22
TradingStatus Byte 1 1 # H halted across all US markets, O halt released into an order acceptance period (IEX-listed), P paused and order acceptance period (IEX-listed), T trading on IEX
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the trading status
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
Reason String 18 4 # T1 IPO1 IPOD MCB3 NA for halts; T2 IPO2 IPO3 MCB1 MCB2 for order acceptance; blank for P and T

MessageType I 0 1 # RetailLiquidityIndicator: change in eligible retail liquidity interest; 0x20 for all symbols before trading (DPLS v1.06, p.17, Retail Liquidity Indicator Message)
@size 18
RetailLiquidityIndicator Byte 1 1 # 0x20 not applicable, A buy interest, B sell interest, C buy and sell interest
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the indicator
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology

MessageType O 0 1 # OperationalHaltStatus: pre-market spin, then changes; absent from the spin means operationally halted (DPLS v1.06, p.18, Operational Halt Status Message)
@size 18
OperationalHaltStatus Byte 1 1 # O IEX operational halt, N not operationally halted
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the operational halt status
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology

MessageType P 0 1 # ShortSalePriceTestStatus: Reg SHO Rule 201 status, pre-market spin then intraday changes (DPLS v1.06, p.19, Short Sale Price Test Status Message)
@size 19
ShortSalePriceTestStatus Byte 1 1 # 0 not in effect, 1 in effect
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the status
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
Detail Byte 18 1 # 0x20 no test, A activated, C continued, D deactivated, N not available (non-IEX-listed)

MessageType E 0 1 # SecurityEvent: opening or closing process complete for a security (DPLS v1.06, p.20, Security Event Message)
@size 18
SecurityEvent Byte 1 1 # O opening process complete, C closing process complete
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the security event
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology

MessageType a 0 1 # AddOrder: a displayed order added to the IEX book (DPLS v1.06, p.21, Add Order Message; type byte changed in v1.01)
@size 38
Side Byte 1 1 # 0x38 '8' buy, 0x35 '5' sell
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the new order
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
OrderID Long 18 8 # Order ID; may be reused by a later Add Order after a delete (p.23)
Size Integer 26 4 # Quoted (displayed) size
Price Price 30 8 # Booking price, 4 implied decimals

MessageType M 0 1 # OrderModify: price, size or priority of a displayed order changed (DPLS v1.06, p.22, Order Modify Message)
@size 38
ModifyFlags Byte 1 1 # Bit 0: 0 reset priority, 1 maintain priority; bits 1-7 reserved
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the modification
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
OrderIDReference Long 18 8 # Order ID from the Add Order
Size Integer 26 4 # New total quoted size
Price Price 30 8 # Booking price, 4 implied decimals

MessageType R 0 1 # OrderDelete: a displayed order removed from the IEX book (DPLS v1.06, p.23, Order Delete Message)
@size 26
Reserved Byte 1 1 # Reserved for future use
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the deletion
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
OrderIDReference Long 18 8 # Order ID from the Add Order

MessageType L 0 1 # OrderExecuted: a displayed order executed against; removed when its quantity reaches 0, otherwise keeps time priority (DPLS v1.06, p.24, Order Executed Message)
@size 46
SaleConditionFlags Byte 1 1 # 0x80 ISO, 0x40 extended hours, 0x20 odd lot, 0x10 trade-through exempt, 0x08 single-price cross (Appendix A, p.28-29)
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the trade
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
OrderIDReference Long 18 8 # Order ID of the resting order executed
Size Integer 26 4 # Trade volume
Price Price 30 8 # Trade price; may differ from the order's displayed price (price improvement, sliding)
TradeID Long 38 8 # IEX generated identifier

MessageType T 0 1 # Trade: a non-displayed order executed against another non-displayed order; no displayed order changes (DPLS v1.06, p.25, Trade Message)
@size 38
SaleConditionFlags Byte 1 1 # As Order Executed (Appendix A)
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the trade
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
Size Integer 18 4 # Trade volume
Price Price 22 8 # Trade price
TradeID Long 30 8 # IEX generated identifier

MessageType B 0 1 # TradeBreak: an execution broken on the same trading day (DPLS v1.06, p.26, Trade Break Message)
@size 38
SaleConditionFlags Byte 1 1 # As Order Executed (Appendix A)
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the trade break
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology
Size Integer 18 4 # Trade break volume
Price Price 22 8 # Trade break price
TradeID Long 30 8 # Trade ID of the Order Executed or Trade message broken

MessageType C 0 1 # ClearBook: the IEX book for a symbol cleared of all orders (DPLS v1.06, p.27, Clear Book Message)
@size 18
Reserved Byte 1 1 # Reserved for future use
Timestamp Timestamp 2 8 # Time of the clear
Symbol String 10 8 # Nasdaq Integrated symbology

### snap::from_iex
@length_prefix 2 exclusive

MessageType e 0 1 # ErrorResponse: the SnapshotRequest was rejected (SNAP v1.07, p.8, ErrorResponse Message; spec Message Length 2)
@size 2
RejectReasonCode Byte 1 1 # Spec offset 3. A authentication, C wrong ChannelID, E request already active, Q quota exceeded, R no snapshot >= Minimum Sequence Number yet, S wrong SessionID, U unknown message

MessageType s 0 1 # SnapshotStart: first message of a snapshot response (SNAP v1.07, p.9, SnapshotStart Message; spec Message Length 9)
@size 9
SnapshotLength Long 1 8 # Spec offset 3. Bytes of the whole response, this SnapshotStart, every SnapshotData and the SnapshotEnd, length prefixes included (example p.9: SnapshotStart counts 11)

MessageType d 0 1 # SnapshotData: one DEEP+ message in an IEX-TP segment with Message Count 1 (SNAP v1.07, p.10, SnapshotData Message)
IEXTPHeader Bytes 1 40 # Spec offset 3. IEX-TP segment header (tp::from_iex SegmentHeader); carries the DEEP+ sequence number and send time
IEXTPMessageBlockLength Short 41 2 # Spec offset 43, typed Integer with length 2. IEX-TP Message Length of the block that follows
IEXTPMessageData Bytes 43 # Spec offset 45. The block's message data; see feed.md section 10 on the extra length in the example (p.10)

MessageType x 0 1 # SnapshotEnd: last message of a snapshot response (SNAP v1.07, p.11, SnapshotEnd Message; spec Message Length 9)
@size 9
SnapshotSequenceNumber Long 1 8 # Spec offset 3. DEEP+ sequence number at which the snapshot was created

### snap::to_iex
@length_prefix 2 exclusive

MessageType r 0 1 # SnapshotRequest: authenticate and request a snapshot; the only client message (SNAP v1.07, p.7, SnapshotRequest Message; spec Message Length 57, total 59)
@size 57
AuthenticationToken Token 1 40 # Spec offset 3. Token from IEX Market Ops, left justified, space padded
ChannelID Integer 41 4 # Spec offset 43. Channel 1-16, from the multicast IEX-TP header
SessionID Integer 45 4 # Spec offset 47. Session, from the multicast IEX-TP header
MinimumSequenceNumber Long 49 8 # Spec offset 51. Lowest snapshot sequence number usable; 0 for the latest snapshot

### end
